:: locked door

 <img src="src/assets/img/rooms/tutorial_exit.jpg" width="800" alt="[]"/>

you are faced with a door with a strange lock. there are 5 shapes: a hexagon, a circle, a triangle, a diamond, and a pentagon. 

[[try the door|lock check]]
[[go back|starting_room]]

investigate the [[hexagon]]
investigate the [[circle]]
investigate the [[triangle]]
investigate the [[diamond]]
investigate the [[pentagon]]

:: lock check

<!--hexagon lock -->
<<if ($heaterNumber == 1) and ($hexagonDial == 9)>>
  <<set $hexagonLock to [True]>>
  the hexagon dial is correct
<</if>>
<<if ($heaterNumber == 2) and ($hexagonDial == 7)>>
  <<set $hexagonLock to [True]>>
  the hexagon dial is correct
<</if>>
<<if ($heaterNumber == 3) and ($hexagonDial == 5)>>
  <<set $hexagonLock to [True]>>
  the hexagon dial is correct
<</if>>
<<if ($heaterNumber == 4) and ($hexagonDial == 3)>>
  <<set $hexagonLock to [True]>>
  the hexagon dial is correct
<</if>>

<!--circle lock -->
<<if ($songNumber == 1) and ($circleDial == 1)>>
<<set $circleLock to [True]>>
the circle dial is correct
<</if>>
<<if ($songNumber == 2) and ($circleDial == 2)>>
<<set $circleLock to [True]>>
the circle dial is correct
<</if>>
<<if ($songNumber == 3) and ($circleDial == 3)>>
<<set $circleLock to [True]>>
the circle dial is correct
<</if>>
<<if ($songNumber == 4) and ($circleDial == 4)>>
<<set $circleLock to [True]>>
the circle dial is correct
<</if>>
